<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizam of Hyderabad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nizam of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a> was the title of the rulers of Hyderabad State in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, a dynasty founded by a former Mughal governor in the early eighteenth century. The Nizams were major rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a>, which fought them repeatedly and imposed tribute arrangements. Hyderabad later became the largest princely state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad.jpg" alt="Nizam of Hyderabad" width="320" height="277" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nizam of Hyderabad, India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hyderabad_Coat_of_Arms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
